Primary key:
(1) Primary key is an unique i1dentifie1r of each roe in the table.
(2) It cannot be null.
(3) Must be unique.
(4) A table can have only one primary key constraint. but it can consist one or multiple columns.
(5) In SQL server primary key create a unique index. By default it is clustered if no cluster index is cretaed.

Eg:
CREATE TABLE Employees
(
    EmployeeId INT PRIMARY KEY,
    Name VARCHAR(50),
    Salary DECIMAL(10, 2)
);

